{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 2, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review as requested. The process involved a meticulous comparison of the entire draft application against the authoritative inventor sources, specifically `input/disclosure.md` and the USER passages within `input/conversation.md`.\n\nFirst, I read all specified files, including the disclosure, conversation, brief, and all draft sections and figure briefs, to build a comprehensive understanding of both the inventor's stated invention and the drafted application.\n\nNext, I constructed a complete source ledger, systematically tracing every technical assertion in the draft back to a specific, affirmative statement in the inventor's source documents. This included:\n*   **Claims:** Each of the 17 claims, including all independent and dependent claims, was dissected, and every single limitation was verified against the disclosure.\n*   **Detailed Description & Numerals:** Every numbered part from `draft/numerals.md` and its corresponding structure, function, and relationship as described in `draft/08-detailed-description.md` was traced to its source. This covered all 28 numbered items from the split pipe clamp (10) to the mounting boss (66).\n*   **Figures:** The descriptions in `draft/07-drawings.md` and the detailed briefs for FIG. 1 through FIG. 6 were checked to ensure they only depict structures and relationships affirmatively disclosed by the inventor. The use of schematic representations was confirmed to be consistent with the rules provided, adding no unsupported technical substance.\n\nFinally, I performed an internal consistency check on the draft itself. This confirmed that terminology is used consistently between the claims and the description, part numerals are unambiguous, figure descriptions align with their briefs, and no drafting notes, placeholders, or unresolved comments remain in the text.\n\nThe review concluded without identifying any disclosure fidelity issues, internal inconsistencies, or other reportable findings. Every element of the draft is properly supported by the inventor's disclosure."}
